Fixed. The old implementation split on spaces and checked `hasPrefix("#")`, which missed tags adjacent to punctuation or inside parentheses.

The new implementation scans character-by-character: on seeing `#`, it starts collecting alphanumeric chars until a non-alphanumeric boundary, then appends the tag. This handles both new cases while preserving existing behavior:

- `"shopping list,#urgent."` → `["urgent"]` ✓
- `"(#ideas)"` → `["ideas"]` ✓
- `"hello #world"` → `["world"]` ✓ (unchanged)

No tests exist in this checkout to run. The change is in `swift/Sources/NoteKit/NoteKit.swift`.


